<v Ken Erwin>No matter-- so the reason that I rolled my eyes is because it's a zero-sum thing. So someone's making money, no matter what. And when they do, that means someone's losing money.
<v Ken Erwin>无论如何——我翻白眼的原因是因为这是一个零和游戏。所以不管怎样，有人赚钱，就意味着有人亏钱。

00:26:21.620 --> 00:26:33.410
<v Ken Erwin>And basically, the earlier you are, the better it is. If you know news before other people, basically, if you're one of these people, you're going to make out really well.
<v Ken Erwin>基本上，你越早介入，情况就越好。如果你比别人先得到消息，基本上，如果你是这些人中的一员，你会赚得很爽。

00:26:33.410 --> 00:26:56.570
<v Ira Glass>And lots of other people, Ken believes, will lose money. What we're seeing in his view is a classic pump and dump, something that if you did it in the stock market would be totally illegal. The apes get in early, talk up Aether on Twitter, encourage other people to buy, which pushes up the price. And in a couple of days when the price is at the highest, they sell, taking a quick and sizeable profit.
<v Ira Glass>而肯认为，还有很多人会亏钱。在他看来，我们所看到的是一个典型的“拉高出货”（pump and dump），如果在股票市场上这样做是完全违法的。“猿群”们尽早介入，在推特上炒作Aether，鼓励其他人购买，从而推高价格。几天后，当价格达到最高点时，他们就卖出，赚取一笔可观的快钱。

