00:27:26.840 --> 00:27:45.560
<v Ira Glass>And that's what Ken thinks is kind of evil about the world of NFTs, why he thinks they're a scam and shouldn't exist. Seeing all this made me wonder if any of this is actually illegal. And I've now talked to a bunch of lawyers about it, lawyers who deal with NFTs and crypto and security fraud, including two who advise companies that release NFTs.
<v Ira Glass>这就是为什么肯认为NFT世界很邪恶，为什么他认为它们是骗局且不应该存在。目睹这一切让我不禁怀疑，这一切是否实际上是违法的。我已经找了几位律师谈过，他们是处理NFT、加密货币和证券欺诈的律师，其中包括两位为发行NFT的公司提供建议的律师。

00:27:45.560 --> 00:28:03.560
<v Ira Glass>And I described what I saw Adam McBride do in relaunching Aether. And all of them told me that NFTs are so new, the law is still pretty vague. There haven't been many lawsuits or much government enforcement in NFTs. But they pointed to two things that could be problematic.
<v Ira Glass>我描述了我所看到的亚当·麦克布莱德在重启Aether时所做的一切。他们所有人都告诉我，NFT太新了，法律还非常模糊。在NFT领域还没出现多少诉讼或政府执法案例。但他们指出了两点可能存在问题的地方。

00:28:03.560 --> 00:28:29.370
<v Ira Glass>OK, first, if Adam and the apes were pumping and dumping-- specifically, if they were lying about Aether or about their own trading, that would be an issue. Like if they were going onto Twitter and telling people that Aether is a great investment, worth seeking money into for the long run, but then if they themselves only held onto it for a few days until the price rose and then they sold it, that would be illegal. That would be market manipulation.
<v Ira Glass>好吧，第一，如果亚当和“猿群”们是在进行“拉高出货”——具体来说，如果他们在关于Aether或他们自己的交易上撒谎，那将是一个问题。就像如果他们去推特上告诉人们Aether是一项伟大的长期投资，值得投入资金，但他们自己却只持有了几天，等到价格上涨就卖掉，那就是违法的。那是市场操纵行为。

00:28:29.370 --> 00:28:44.000
<v Ira Glass>The second thing the lawyers pointed to, transparency is key. If Adam was going out giving a special price to 50 people to generate buzz and excitement, that is a normal kind of promotion in lots of industries, one of the lawyers says. He said that could be fine.
<v Ira Glass>律师指出的第二件事是，透明度是关键。如果亚当出去给50个人一个特别价格以创造热度和兴奋感，这是一位律师所说的许多行业中常见的一种促销行为。他说那可能没问题。

00:28:44.000 --> 00:29:04.160
<v Ira Glass>But the key to that being OK is that Adam would need to disclose it all publicly so that any possible investor can find out that some people got a special cheaper price. If Adam didn't do that, he would be in danger of some investor, maybe somebody who lost money, later suing him over holding back that information.
<v Ira Glass>但这一切没问题的关键在于，亚当需要公开披露这一切，以便任何可能的投资者都能发现有些人得到了特别的低价。如果亚当没这么做，他就有可能面临投资者的诉讼，也许是亏钱的人，后来因为他隐瞒了这些信息而起诉他。

00:29:04.160 --> 00:29:18.900
<v Ira Glass>OK, so was Adam crossing the line into illegality with either of those things? Ken still didn't have proof of that, either way.
